{
    "background_story": "Rowyn was a wise and weathered tortoise who spent most of his days basking in the warm sun of the desert landscape. As the summer months approached, the temperatures soared, and the land grew dry and cracked. Rowyn, sensing the change, began to prepare for his annual estivation. He slowly made his way to his favorite burrow, a hidden sanctuary beneath the roots of an ancient mesquite tree. There, he sealed himself within, wrapping his body in a protective layer of skin and mucous. As the blistering heat raged above, Rowyn rested, his metabolism slowing to a crawl. For months, he remained in this state of dormancy, conserving energy and waiting for the cooler rains to revive the parched landscape. When the seasons finally shifted, Rowyn emerged, refreshed and renewed, ready to take on another year of exploring the desert's vast expanse.",
